 ## Overview
-Volumetric representation defines a 3D scene as a continuous or discrete scalar function $F(x,y,z)$ that assigns a value to every point in space, capturing internal density variations rather than just boundaries [S2, S1, unofficial]. Unlike surface-based representations which define only boundaries, this method models the entire volume's properties [S2, unofficial]. It builds on [Procedural and implicit volumes](13-procedural-and-implicit-volumes.md) by providing the underlying mathematical field that procedural methods populate.
